            <ArticleTitle>A C-H Oxidation/Two-Fold Cyclization Approach to Imidazopyridoindole Scaffold under Mild Oxidizing Conditions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13671-13677</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.joc.7b02448</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An expeditious one-step synthesis of the imidazopyridoindole scaffold was achieved through the C-H oxidation/two-fold cyclization reaction of methyl ketone and tryptamine derivatives. Mild oxidizing conditions were employed to realize the efficient oxidation of C(sp3)-H bonds, while suppressing overoxidation of the intermediate and ensuring the cross-trapping of two in situ generated acylimine intermediates.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
